<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Guilds (system: crafting, tracker item crafting.guilds). A guild is the civilization-scale form of
    RimWorld's workbench bill queue: the bills are unchanged, but the stack belongs to a settlement, the
    ingredients come from that settlement's stores and the members are its citizens carrying the guild's
    RoleDef.

    One guild ships, and deliberately only one. A guild's recipes must have fixed ingredients — a settlement
    holds a def-count ledger, not a stockpile it can choose between candidates in (see Guild's own remarks) —
    and Make_Blocks_Sandstone is the only shipped recipe that qualifies. Cooking's recipes all draw on
    category filters ("any meat", "any raw plant food"), so a cooks' guild waits on a settlement stock model
    that can make that choice rather than on new content here.
  -->

  <GuildDef>
    <defName>MasonsGuild</defName>
    <label>masons' guild</label>
    <description>Cuts quarried stone into building blocks. The first industry a settlement that has stopped moving tends to want, and the one whose output the next age is built out of.</description>
    <role>Artisan</role>
    <skill>Crafting</skill>
    <recipes>
      <li>Make_Blocks_Sandstone</li>
    </recipes>
  </GuildDef>

</Defs>
